  "proof_summary": [
    "The actual positive reference density formulas give a=H^2*w*Yprime, b=0 and c=H^2/Yprime*(wprime/r). Genuine inverse differentiation gives chi-prime=(Yprime o chi)^-1 and hence the exact inverse-a and c scalar expressions.",
    "For the same whole V, positive canonical endpoints are0/1, so its actual canonicalUnitPoint is literally the identity. The four stored atoms agree with these radial expressions on the actual unitStrip, without assumptions on arbitrary total extensions outside it.",
    "Open-set equality gives all mixed jets. Smoothness at each inverse image uses physical w>0 and r>0 on the real positive component; period follows from the same radial formula.",
    "The fixed163 material provider supplies all three nonzero scalar jet bounds for the supplied C0/cell/Y/H. A finite prefix and coefficientEnvelope_pack give a single B for all four atoms and a+b<=s. The explicit unscaled sample floor is assumed after normalization, and the very same T occurs in V and the final bound."
